:!: [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/hootoo-ht-tm01-how-to-flash-stock-firmware/31436/95|Likely]], using the official OpenWRT files ''initramfs-kernel.bin'' resp. ''squashfs-sysupgrade.bin'' above will overwrite the ''params'' partition (one of the device specific partitions) and softbrick the device. 

There are two community builds available: 
  * wingspinner's 15.05 image is described on the [[:toh:hootoo:tripmate-nano|Tripmate OpenWRT page]]
    * can be used for initial flashing from vendor UI
    * but introduces a few **[[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/hootoo-ht-tm01-how-to-flash-stock-firmware/31436/67|unrecoverable modifications]]** to the device
    * **can be upgraded to the official images above**.
  * [[https://forum.openwrt.org/u/xabolcs|xabolcs]]'s 19.07 ''kernel.bin'' and ''rootfs.bin'' files:
    * use only the stock 1536 k ''Kernel_RootFS'' and the 6144 k ''​Rootfs'' partitions.
    * they're installable through the vendor U-Boot's TFTP recovery on the TM02 as well as the TM01, and
    * compatible (read: the kmods are installable) with the official OpenWrt releases (currently 19.07.7)
    * **avoid cross upgrades between this and official OpenWrt or wingspinnner's firmwares**! 
    * support forum: [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/xabolcs-custom-builds-for-ramips-rt305x-sunvalleytek-tripmate-devices-stock-compatible-flash-layout-for-hootoo-ht-tm01-ht-tm02-and-ravpower-rp-wd02/103367?u=xabolcs|@xabolcs' custom builds for ramips/rt305x Sunvalleytek Tripmate devices: stock compatible flash layout for HooToo HT-TM01, HT-TM02 and RAVPower RP-WD02]]

A [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/hootoo-ht-tm01-how-to-flash-stock-firmware/31436/67|more detailed comparison]] is given in the forum.

xabolcs's files for the TM02 can be installed on the TM01 from stock FW as follows, using a TFTP server on another computer that has a free LAN port:

  - to create a system backup first, write file ''EnterRouterMode.sh'' from [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/hootoo-ht-tm01-how-to-flash-stock-firmware/31436/50|here]] to a USB stick (needs not be empty), and insert it to the TM01 while it's running.  This script will create a new folder on the USB stick with copies of the TM01's original partitions.
  - set your computer's LAN port to a fixed IP address ''10.10.10.254'' with subnet ''255.255.255.0''.
  - optionally set up Wireshark on your computer to listen to this LAN port.
  - prepare the TFTP server on your computer (e.g. Apple's built-in TFTP server), and place xabolcs's [[https://github.com/xabolcs/openwrt_hootoo_ht-tm02_oldstable/releases/tag/v19.07.7-0|two files]] ''kernel.bin'' and ''rootfs.bin'' into the TFTP server's root directory. The other files there are not needed.
  - In your TFTP server's folder, name these files ''kernel'' and ''rootfs'', without the ''.bin'' extension. Note that these are 'random binaries from the internet' (namely, from xabolcs's [[https://github.com/xabolcs/openwrt_hootoo_ht-tm02_oldstable|github project]]).
  - Power off the router, connect everything (via switch or direct), start your TFTP server, and monitor traffic in Wireshark if needed. 
  - Press and hold router reset pin with paper clip. While holding reset then press and hold router power button. Wifi LED should light up then go out again, 3-5 seconds.
  - Continue holding reset and release power. After another 10-15 seconds you should see ''10.10.10.128'' looking for tftp on ''10.10.10.254''. Now you can release the reset pin.
  - when the TM01 reboots after flashing (should be few minutes at max), change your computer's fixed LAN address to ''192.168.1.2'' in order to reach OpenWRT on your TM01 at ''192.168.1.1'' (e.g. LuCI).
  - configure OpenWRT on your TM01 as you like --- and don't forget to configure your computer's LAN port back to normal.

